{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Blessed above sons is Asher</b> Therefore Moses blessed him with these words, because when the tribes sold Joseph they imposed a ban [herem] that no one reveal it, and Serah daughter of Asher knew of the sale through prophecy, and the tribes said: From where did she know if not from her father? Because of a child's chatter — either from father or from mother — they arose and excommunicated him [Asher]. And Moses our Master came and permitted him [lifted the ban]. For one who is excommunicated is forbidden in marital relations — so he said: <b>Blessed above sons</b>. His brothers were distancing themselves from him — so he said: <b>and acceptable to his brothers</b>. He was forbidden in anointing — so he said: <b>and he dips his foot in oil</b>, that he be permitted to anoint with oil. He was forbidden in the wearing of a sandal — so he said: <b>Iron and copper your shoe</b>." "<b>From sons Asher acceptable</b> ראשי תיבות מאיר. On account of the oil, for it illuminates the face. And [it is] מאיר for the Menorah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:31.060903424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}